  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Cool weather and periods of showers will continue \nthrough tonight.\n\nA mid level closed low will drift southeast across New York State \ntoday. The associated surface low just north of Lake Ontario this \nmorning will redevelop as a coastal wave downstream this afternoon. \nThis will bring the likelihood of showers as moisture pivots into\nthe region. The greatest coverage of showers will be underneath\nthe mid level low across western New York with lesser coverage \nor even dry weather across the eastern Lake Ontario region as a \ndry slot works into that area on the eastern side of the low.\n\nThe greater coverage of showers tonight will shift into the eastern \nLake Ontario region as the mid level low drifts to the southeast and \nAtlantic moisture pivots westward around the northern periphery of \nthe low. Additional rainfall amounts will be light. Rain chances \nmostly end across western New York as drier high pressure ridges in \nfrom the southwest.\n\nWell below normal temperatures are expected today, with highs only \nin the lower to mid 50s for lower elevations and upper 40s for \nhigher terrain, close to 15 degrees below average. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A notable warming trend will start Friday, then \ngains momentum over the weekend with summer-like heat by early next \nweek.\n\nA notable warming trend will start Friday, but persistent warm \nadvection will bring an extended period of above average warmth over \nthe weekend, lasting through at least Tuesday. Highs over the \nweekend will be in the 70s, with 80s for Monday and Tuesday away\nfrom lake influences. Some of the normally warmer locations may\nreach the upper 80s to lower 90s Monday and Tuesday.",
